Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 1 year after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Article 13-2(6) shall enter into force 1 year and 6 months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Transitional measures regarding requirements for operating special means of transportation)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 16-4(1), drivers operating special means of transportation at the time of this Act enters into force shall meet the requirements for persons operating the special means of transportation under the amended provisions within 1 year from the date this Act enters into force. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2024>
(2) Where any person who is employed as a driver operating special means of transportation by an institution or organization entrusted with the operation of a mobility support center or a multi-regional mobility support center in accordance with Article 16(11) at the time this Act enters into force falls under the grounds for restriction on employment under the amended provisions of Article 16-4(2) of this Act due to reasons that occurred before the enforcement of this Act, notwithstanding those amended provisions, the previous provisions shall apply until such person is employed by the relevant local government or the entrusted institution or organization. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2024>

